  "body": "Closes the finding `operator_review` raised four times: the dev-node lane could not be found at any canonical path, because it only ever existed in a scratch tree on the development host.\n\n## What lands\n\n| Path | Why |\n| --- | --- |\n| `devnode/README.md` | Why the lane cannot be hosted, and two things about this console a future test author would otherwise rediscover the hard way |\n| `devnode/tui/{Cargo.toml,Cargo.lock,tests/tui.rs}` | Eight TUIWright flows driving the **installed** `bullet` binary through a real pseudo-terminal |\n| `ops/ci/devnode.sh` | The lane driver: typed refusals for every missing prerequisite, both Playwright halves mandatory |\n| `scripts/ci-local.sh`, `ops/ci/artifact-check.sh`, `scripts/ci-doctor.sh` | Lane registry entries |\n| `ops/ci/workflow-policy.sh` + test | The hosted-refusal guard and its hostile fixtures |\n| `ops/ci/lib.sh` + `ops/ci/rust-build-subject-test.sh` | Proof-only manifest classification |\n\n## The manifest question, resolved the way the reviewers asked\n\nMy first attempt pruned `./devnode` from the build-subject search. Both reviewers rejected it, and they were right \u2014 pruning would have made every future manifest under that directory invisible to the guard.\n\nThere are now two pinned classes. Product manifests are what ships. Proof manifests belong to harnesses that are never a product dependency and are built by no lane other than the one they prove; `crates/bullet-wire/fuzz/Cargo.toml` set the precedent and `devnode/tui/Cargo.toml` joins it. Both the manifest and its lock are digest-pinned exactly as a product manifest is.\n\n**The four product manifest pins and the seven existing subject pins are byte-identical to main.**\n\nFour new canary cases cover precisely what pruning would have let through:\n\n- a second harness beside the pinned one \u2192 `CARGO_MANIFEST_INVENTORY_DRIFT`\n- the pinned harness removed \u2192 `CARGO_MANIFEST_INVENTORY_DRIFT`\n- a changed harness dependency \u2192 `RUST_BUILD_SUBJECT_DRIFT`\n- a changed harness lock \u2192 `RUST_BUILD_SUBJECT_DRIFT`\n\n## Why the lane refuses to be hosted\n\nIt drives the real console and the real browser against an authenticated operator session. That session and the provider credentials behind it exist on one machine. A hosted copy could only ever prove something weaker while carrying the name of a lane that claims much more, so it is refused twice: `ops/ci/devnode.sh` refuses under `GITHUB_ACTIONS`, and `ops/ci/workflow-policy.sh` refuses any hosted workflow that names it. The second guard has hostile fixtures for a job that runs the lane, a commented-out mention, a matrix entry, and a symlinked workflow entry.\n\n## Proved locally before pushing\n\n- the full `lint` lane passes end to end\n- the build-subject canary passes, and fails with `RUST_BUILD_SUBJECT_DRIFT` when the new pin is falsified\n- the workflow policy passes, and fails with `WORKFLOW_DEVNODE_HOSTILE_FAILED` when the devnode guard is neutered\n\nsha256, `LC_ALL=C`, of each new file:\n\n```\n9a266726781bdaa5d38fb92b00e371b9dde61a3baae6616be4e25c28a3b2c01a  devnode/README.md\ne7de1ce77d1c5573bd0b53edbf55aa9cb3b21979bff8aa18244597f222b61a31  devnode/tui/Cargo.toml\nefa9e735ab167412e00f1fe184b83026d62f317a2d9bbd51dba7576365908401  devnode/tui/Cargo.lock\naf7f9f56a9eef28d9f9c65dad27097e3882c2bc7bcc867691ee95ceeefea75c5  devnode/tui/tests/tui.rs\nef1958731bdf7a7bef45afe7824fb25fd962f7dbafadbd4f78b5652c68153d2e  ops/ci/devnode.sh\n```\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_015qHQABNS382h2gi5jb5oUY\n",
